{"id": "wwdc2017-812", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2017/812", "wordCount": 1242, "segments": [{"start": 21.0, "text": "So, designing for iOS used to"}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "be a lot more simple."}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "There was only one phone."}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "We now have three different"}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "screen sizes for iPhone and"}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "three iPad sizes, with different"}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "orientations, and split screens,"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "and multitasking screens."}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "And that might seem like a lot"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "of different screen sizes to"}, {"start": 42.0, "text": "consider, but there's a basic"}, {"start": 44.0, "text": "framework for designing and"}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "building your app that"}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "simplifies the process."}, {"start": 49.0, "text": "This will save you time and your"}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "app will look great regardless"}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "of what device people are using."}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "The key things to consider are"}, {"start": 58.0, "text": "organizing your screens into"}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "size classes, using Dynamic"}, {"start": 63.0, "text": "Type, and taking advantage of"}, {"start": 66.0, "text": "standard UI elements."}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "And all of these things are"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "meant to make it easier for you"}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "to design and build your app."}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "So, first let's take a look at"}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "size classes."}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "All screen sizes -- all iOS"}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "screen dimensions fall under one"}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "of two size classes, compact or"}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "regular."}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "And an easy way to think about"}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "this is that the narrower screen"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "widths are compact size, like an"}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "iPhone layout."}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "And a wider screen widths are"}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "regular like the width of an"}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "iPad."}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "If you stack all of the screens"}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "on top of each other, in both"}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "portrait and in landscape"}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "orientations you can see that"}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "size class applies to both width"}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "and height."}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "The goal of creating these two"}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "size classes is so that layouts"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "will be flexible and elements"}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "will adapt relative to their"}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "screen size."}, {"start": 118.0, "text": "So let me give you a couple"}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "examples of what that might"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "potentially mean for your"}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "layout."}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "The iPhone 7 Plus in landscape,"}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "falls under regular width, which"}, {"start": 129.0, "text": "allows it to use Split Views"}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "like all of the iPads."}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "And the two smaller phones in"}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "landscape are compact in both"}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "width and height. This means they will get shorter"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "landscape bar heights than the"}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "standard height that you see in"}, {"start": 145.0, "text": "portrait."}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "Screen widths also define UIKit"}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "margins and margin, the margin"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "widths can either be standard or"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "like this iPad generous for"}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "wider screens."}, {"start": 159.0, "text": "But in this example and a lot of"}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "other cases, text, if text went"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "edge to edge with the UIKit"}, {"start": 165.0, "text": "margins then the lines of text"}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "would be too long making it hard"}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "for the eye to jump down when"}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "you get to the end of a line."}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "So, we use readability margins"}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "to restrict the line lengths on"}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "larger devices."}, {"start": 180.0, "text": "These margins are flexible"}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "because they can vary with the"}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "text size."}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "And smaller text needs more"}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "narrow readability lengths, and"}, {"start": 188.0, "text": "larger text can have longer"}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "lengths."}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "And if you're using Dynamic Type"}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "with readability margins, then"}, {"start": 194.0, "text": "people using your app will have"}, {"start": 196.0, "text": "a much more comfortable reading"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "experience."}, {"start": 199.0, "text": "So, let's talk more about"}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "Dynamic Type, what it is and how"}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "it can help people use your app."}, {"start": 207.0, "text": "Dynamic Type are predefined text"}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "styles that can be scaled on a"}, {"start": 211.0, "text": "device so that people can see"}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "text at a size that is most"}, {"start": 215.0, "text": "comfortable for them."}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "And there are a lot of people"}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "who find text in their apps to"}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "be way too small to read."}, {"start": 222.0, "text": "So, using Dynamic Type will"}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "automatically allow text to"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "scale up or down without"}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "compromising your layout."}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "And it also makes opting in"}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "Accessibility Settings for even"}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "larger type, much easier."}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "It also makes localizing your"}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "app seamless."}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "Your text will adjust the"}, {"start": 241.0, "text": "lettering, or line height based"}, {"start": 243.0, "text": "on the height of the characters."}, {"start": 245.0, "text": "So using these features will"}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "only make it easier for more"}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "people to use your app."}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "So, this is our Dynamic Type"}, {"start": 252.0, "text": "chart."}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "And this year, we've made some"}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "adjustments to our existing text"}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "styles by increasing the weight"}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "of Title sizes from light to"}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "regular."}, {"start": 262.0, "text": "In most cases, we recommend"}, {"start": 264.0, "text": "using two to three of these text"}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "styles per screen."}, {"start": 269.0, "text": "But with ten different text"}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "styles to choose from, there are"}, {"start": 272.0, "text": "countless combinations and a lot"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "of flexibility when you're"}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "designing your app."}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "The names of the text styles are"}, {"start": 279.0, "text": "meant to be descriptive,"}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "suggesting where certain styles"}, {"start": 283.0, "text": "are most appropriately used."}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "So for instance, Body is"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "intended to be used in places"}, {"start": 289.0, "text": "where large bodies of text are"}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "needed."}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "And Body is also the default"}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "that we use throughout the"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "system."}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "And from there, we can introduce"}, {"start": 298.0, "text": "smaller and larger styles, or in"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "this case bolder, to create"}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "hierarchy."}, {"start": 305.0, "text": "But what if you're using a"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "custom font in your design?"}, {"start": 309.0, "text": "So, this year, with our new API"}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "we have, we can make custom"}, {"start": 313.0, "text": "fonts Dynamic as well, which is"}, {"start": 315.0, "text": "great."}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "Keep in mind that you may have"}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "to design -- assign different"}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "point sizes for each text style"}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "because not all fonts have the"}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "same proportions."}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "And this is important for"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "keeping your text optically the"}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "same size."}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "Etsy is a good example of an app"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "that uses Dynamic Type."}, {"start": 333.0, "text": "Here it is at its default size,"}, {"start": 336.0, "text": "and here it is at a much larger"}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "size, and it looks great."}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "So, last but not least, let's"}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "discuss UIKit Elements."}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "Rather than focusing effort on"}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "designing a task or function"}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "that people are already familiar"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "with, we want you to be able to"}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "focus your time designing what"}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "makes your app unique."}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "We have a bunch of standard UI"}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "elements that you can use in"}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "your app that will automatically"}, {"start": 362.0, "text": "adapt on all screen sizes."}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "So, this includes things like"}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "TableViews which not only scale"}, {"start": 368.0, "text": "nicely with Dynamic Type, it"}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "also inherits readability"}, {"start": 371.0, "text": "margins and standard"}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "interactions, like swipe"}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "actions, and edit mode."}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "And there are a lot of other"}, {"start": 378.0, "text": "resources that will help enforce"}, {"start": 380.0, "text": "consistency and adapt seamlessly"}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "across devices."}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "It's important to note that all"}, {"start": 386.0, "text": "of these components are scaled"}, {"start": 388.0, "text": "for iOS 7, which is the size"}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "that we recommend you start a"}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "new design."}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "Once you have an iPhone design"}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "we have a couple tips for"}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "adapting it to iPad."}, {"start": 401.0, "text": "So, going back for a minute, we"}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "now know that regular size"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "classes or iPads can use Split"}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "Views and to maintain content"}, {"start": 409.0, "text": "hierarchy between iPhone and"}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "iPad consider how your app will"}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "relay out."}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "The left side of the Split View"}, {"start": 417.0, "text": "can be referred to as the Master"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "View."}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "And on the right is the Detail"}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "View. And the Detail View on an iPhone"}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "would be the page you have to"}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "drill down further to see."}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "Remember, an iPad will share"}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "both iPad and iPhone specific"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "layouts and iPad layouts should"}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "maintain the same level of"}, {"start": 438.0, "text": "hierarchy as the iPhone layout"}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "including standard navigation,"}, {"start": 442.0, "text": "toolbars, and tab bars."}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "If your app has enabled"}, {"start": 446.0, "text": "multitasking, this will create"}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "consistency when your app has to"}, {"start": 450.0, "text": "coexist with another app."}, {"start": 453.0, "text": "And while in multitasking your"}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "app will transition back and"}, {"start": 456.0, "text": "forth between the iPhone layout"}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "or compact, and back to regular"}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "size classes depending on its"}, {"start": 464.0, "text": "current screen width."}, {"start": 466.0, "text": "Okay, so to recap."}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "When designing for iOS, it's"}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "important to keep these three"}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "things in mind."}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "Considering size class will make"}, {"start": 475.0, "text": "your app look amazing regardless"}, {"start": 478.0, "text": "of what device people are using."}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "Using Dynamic Type will make it"}, {"start": 483.0, "text": "easy for your text to scale and"}, {"start": 486.0, "text": "translate to different languages, and this will enable"}, {"start": 489.0, "text": "more people to use your app."}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "And taking advantage of existing"}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "UI elements will free you up"}, {"start": 495.0, "text": "from redesigning and rebuilding"}, {"start": 497.0, "text": "features that people might"}, {"start": 499.0, "text": "already be familiar with."}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "We encourage you to take"}, {"start": 502.0, "text": "advantage of these tools, not"}, {"start": 504.0, "text": "only to save you time, but so"}, {"start": 506.0, "text": "that regardless of what iOS app"}, {"start": 509.0, "text": "people are using, your app"}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "experience will be seamless."}]}